OL,3,GNEWSAMore than 140 authors sign letter
OL,4,Araising concerns over libraries
OL,5,Aproposals
OL,6,
OL,7,FMore than 140 writers and illustrators
OL,8,Fhave signed an open letter raising
OL,9,Fconcerns about plans for Northern
OL,10,FIreland's public libraries.
OL,12,FThe signatories, who include Oliver
OL,13,FJeffers, Jan Carson, Wendy Erskine and
OL,14,FLucy Caldwell, said they are concerned
OL,15,Fthe proposals "could pave the way for
OL,16,Fbook bans, restrictions for minority
OL,17,Fgroup visibility and library closures".
OL,19,FCommunities Minister Gordon Lyons said
OL,20,Flibrarians would decide which books to
OL,21,Fstock and that he wanted libraries to
OL,22,Fremain "open to all on the same basis".
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
